sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/delphisci-swarm-02-single-agent-shortfall-is-mostly-blank-plans> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Where the single agent fell short of 20 verified datasets, it was mostly because it left plans blank rather than because it named datasets that failed verification (8 of 8 shortfalls blank in experiment 2; 3 blank and 4 named-but-unverified of 7 in experiment 1)." ;
    dct:description "Per-claim triage of the single agent's primary runs. Experiment 2 (fetch required): 12 verified, shortfall 8; blank plans (dataset null with a reason) 8 [darwin1859-ch05-06, darwin1859-ch04-22, darwin1859-ch11-01, darwin1859-ch14-03, darwin1859-ch12-05, thompson1917-ch07-04, thompson1917-ch17-06, thompson1917-ch13-02]; named datasets that failed verification 0. The single agent made 13 WebFetch and 5 WebSearch calls for 20 claims in one context (centralized arm: 35 fetches over 26 calls) and produced 13589 output tokens against the centralized arm's 64948. Experiment 1 (from memory): 13 verified, shortfall 7; blank 3 [thompson1917-ch15-01, thompson1917-ch14-02, thompson1917-ch05-24]; named-but-unverified 4 [darwin1859-ch12-08, darwin1859-ch12-09, darwin1859-ch12-04, darwin1859-ch12-10]; output tokens 25177 vs 74946. So in experiment 2 the whole shortfall was blanks, and in experiment 1 about half of it was." ;
    delphi:context "Task: for each of 20 claims from Darwin (1859) and Thompson (1917), write a pre-registered test plan naming one real public dataset (landing URL, DOI if any) or an honest null. Arms: single agent (one call, all 20 claims), isolated workers (20 parallel, no feedback), centralized swarm (emperor sets concurrency, king assigns by domain, retries with verifier feedback, escalation), decentralized board (queens pull tickets from a shared board, no planner). Same model (claude-sonnet-5-5), same tools (WebFetch, WebSearch), same prompt and schema, run from an empty directory with no file access. Experiment 1 (2026-10-31T05:57Z): plans could be written from memory; budget $3 soft cap per arm; \"verified\" = the named landing page returns HTTP 200 and contains a distinctive token of the dataset or publisher name. Experiment 2 (2026-10-31T06:28Z): 20 new claims with no bird claims; the agent had to fetch the landing page itself (checked in the CLI event log) and report a title that agrees with the checker's; hard $8 cap that cannot overshoot. Pre-registered decision rule: an arm beats another only with zero fabricated identifiers and at least two more verified datasets; the earliest full run per arm is primary. Fabricated = URL or DOI that returns 404/410, DNS failure or \"DOI not found\"; blocked (403, 429, 5xx, timeout) is not fabricated." ;
    skos:note "Status: supported for experiment 2; mixed for experiment 1, where 4 of 7 shortfalls were datasets the single agent named that did not check out, so it also chose worse there. This triage is a post-hoc breakdown of pre-registered runs: the runs, the claim sets and the scoring rule were fixed in advance, but the blank-versus-wrong split was computed after the results were known, prompted by a question from the hub on 2026-10-31. Treat it as exploratory. Pre-registration timing, stated here because the header of swarm/PREREG.md is wrong: the header says \"Written 2026-10-31 06:25 UTC\", which would be after the experiment-1 runs. The session transcript shows the file written at 2026-10-31T05:52:04Z, before the first primary run started at 2026-10-31T05:57:46.622Z; the experiment-2 section was appended at 2026-10-31T06:27:23Z, before the first experiment-2 run at 2026-10-31T06:28:12.756Z. The file was not edited because it states it is never changed after runs start; the correction is in DEVIATIONS.md and here. No git commit of the file exists yet (the hub holds all commits for this branch); the commit hash is to be added to this record before signing." ;
    skos:scopeNote "What this does not establish. (1) It does not identify the mechanism: \"attention\" or \"context limit\" is an interpretation of blank plans; no ablation of context length or turn cap (60 turns in experiment 1, 250 in experiment 2 for the single arm) was run, and a blank can also be a choice the agent made under those caps. (2) The hypothesis was not pre-registered; the counts are exact but the reading is post hoc. (3) It is specific to language-model agents: A sister project (delphi-evolve, github.com/kganjam/delphi-evolve) ran the same four-arm design on an enzyme benchmark with deterministic specialists and found no collective advantage (sharing 78/100, isolated 77/100, single planner 78/100, single planner without its model prior 96/100; zero false certificates); those numbers are quoted from the hub and were not re-verified by this thread. (4) Twenty claims per experiment, one primary run each. (5) The centralized swarm's own one blank per experiment is not analysed here." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/delphisci-swarm-02-single-agent-shortfall-is-mostly-blank-plans> .
}

